inhalt.text:
After losing the election, the government peacefully hands power to the winner. {{1}}
A secret police force monitors those who criticise the government and has people arrested without a court ruling. {{2}}
Newspapers may only print what the party permits. {{3}}
A court declares a government law invalid – and the government abides by the ruling. {{4}}
Only one party is allowed; all others are banned. {{5}}
An opposition party criticises the government in parliament and stands in the next election. {{6}}
Everyone entitled to vote can do so freely, in secret and without pressure. {{7}}
The government makes laws alone – parliament no longer has a say. {{8}}
